# Write a short imperative summary on the first line.
# Then fill the declaration fields below.
#
# Allowed values:
# - Change-Type: behavior | internal | docs | refactor
# - Behavior-Doc: docs/product/... | n/a
# - Tests-Updated: yes | no | n/a
# - Approval: explicit | n/a
# - Approval-Source: path-or-note | n/a
#
# Notes:
# - Use Change-Type: behavior only when implementing or changing human-approved behavior.
# - Behavior commits must reference the canonical behavior doc and update tests in the same change.
# - Use Approval: explicit only when a human explicitly approved the behavior change.
# - When Approval is explicit, Approval-Source must point to the approval artifact or note.

Change-Type: <behavior|internal|docs|refactor>
Behavior-Doc: <docs/product/...|n/a>
Tests-Updated: <yes|no|n/a>
Approval: <explicit|n/a>
Approval-Source: <path-or-note|n/a>
